{"id": "clm:b02a136744b95bb9568a1f94677cf3a091e43a446d88a1c93f7148895ac4099f", "type": "statement", "text": "The documented success payload is an array containing orgId, resourceId, resourceName, resourceType, and resourcePoliciesCausingNonCompliance; nested entries identify resourcePolicyId, resourcePolicyName, and policiesCausingNonCompliance[].policyId. (medium confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-23)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/api/doc/atlas-admin-api-v2/operation/operation-getorgnoncompliantresources", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Atlas nonCompliantResources endpoint"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "definition", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.withone.ai/knowledge/mongo-db-atlas-administration/conn_mod_def%3A%3AGJ4_1NI5agE%3A%3AFIuB2LCpSeirBrBvHRVLQQ"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:0320a8ff506dc89ab56472dec931f5fddb4fabd7101e4f8addd28b61fcace06c", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:ad3105985ebe097dc97d66ca4ba85d2d2a8e18e48fe73279a9e30e0530cf3c94"]}
{"id": "clm:a632ec251bcdde8fbd4b73da9efa38ca99538886b55be5e73eefc7836bf8da29", "type": "statement", "text": "MongoDB recommends proactively monitoring this endpoint because resource policies do not enforce all intermediate or transitional states; downstream failures can leave a temporary non-compliant state. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/atlas-resource-policies.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Atlas nonCompliantResources endpoint"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "mechanism", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:0320a8ff506dc89ab56472dec931f5fddb4fabd7101e4f8addd28b61fcace06c", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:5044ae0b6ae91e3bc373353cc33b3ea1356268bdf9b231b802e6d3f0b4ede00e"]}
{"id": "clm:78961bcfea64e8d50bbbf4e6e56921e949338d65178536b85b53282004101899", "type": "statement", "text": "A practical monitoring pattern is to poll this endpoint, feed results into configuration-drift alerting, and track remediation or documented exceptions; this is operational guidance rather than a documented push-notification feature. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://howtoharden.com/guides/mongodb-atlas/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Atlas nonCompliantResources endpoint"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "comparisons", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/atlas-resource-policies.md"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:0320a8ff506dc89ab56472dec931f5fddb4fabd7101e4f8addd28b61fcace06c", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:5044ae0b6ae91e3bc373353cc33b3ea1356268bdf9b231b802e6d3f0b4ede00e", "ev:5e5b9972d82be3ecd76b3282345dd989702f927178d185d1e9215bc9ec45c96d"]}
{"id": "clm:1586f0a49e2622c277e9f96082c529d60022ac8a55a6ce0a76535939bf878803", "type": "statement", "text": "GET /api/atlas/v2/orgs/{orgId}/nonCompliantResources returns non-compliant resources for an organization; MongoDB’s Go SDK index exposes the same route as GetNonCompliantResources. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/api/doc/atlas-admin-api-v2/operation/operation-getorgnoncompliantresources", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Atlas nonCompliantResources endpoint"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://github.com/mongodb/atlas-sdk-go/blob/main/docs/doc_last_reference.md", "https://foojay.io/today/enforcing-governance-in-mongodb-atlas-with-resource-policies/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:0320a8ff506dc89ab56472dec931f5fddb4fabd7101e4f8addd28b61fcace06c", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:876757b7c35b8af52998abcd593ad187e114dfb6a3e6669e5dcea354aaf676bc", "ev:b0b690cdc116e45874378065d2ee3220b35dbaf18c86ef53199a4e0b3ff8ba29"]}
{"id": "clm:6f60620cd0cc8db51a4d3c9acf1ffeded8145493786fc64cac506595d915de09", "type": "statement", "text": "The API reference lists Organization Member as the role requirement. orgId is required and is a 24-hexadecimal string. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-23)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/api/doc/atlas-admin-api-v2/operation/operation-getorgnoncompliantresources", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Atlas nonCompliantResources endpoint"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:0320a8ff506dc89ab56472dec931f5fddb4fabd7101e4f8addd28b61fcace06c", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:b0b690cdc116e45874378065d2ee3220b35dbaf18c86ef53199a4e0b3ff8ba29"]}
{"id": "clm:d2c79fed33734771d83e4f3031fcc5aa31ba8ab2a44575cbad9d58144fc1ad07", "type": "statement", "text": "The documented resourceType values are PROJECT, CLUSTER, DEPRECATED_PROJECT and DEPRECATED_CLUSTER; do not assume a separate NETWORK enum from informal descriptions of network violations. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-23)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/api/doc/atlas-admin-api-v2/operation/operation-getorgnoncompliantresources", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Atlas nonCompliantResources endpoint"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:0320a8ff506dc89ab56472dec931f5fddb4fabd7101e4f8addd28b61fcace06c", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:49edd59ff5b280ffde66ce78594f787dff3c0be5b6e28b264a4f93cfebac8abb"]}
{"id": "clm:bcae7d427dd5a22d1c4349d71a9127f77788c742cce4b1bb9879dfd5061a77eb", "type": "statement", "text": "The endpoint documents envelope and pretty boolean query options, both defaulting to false. Its default response example is a JSON array. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-23)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/api/doc/atlas-admin-api-v2/operation/operation-getorgnoncompliantresources", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Atlas nonCompliantResources endpoint"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:0320a8ff506dc89ab56472dec931f5fddb4fabd7101e4f8addd28b61fcace06c", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:ad3105985ebe097dc97d66ca4ba85d2d2a8e18e48fe73279a9e30e0530cf3c94", "ev:d83de2dce6469b90f793f4e1c7ffd66c9376877341a9fcdcf7cd97b6da0c1da5"]}
{"id": "clm:c3a5fd32ffd12a9dfeacf62e4220333be03fd80ef702b38ce1e6d8acfcad1166", "type": "statement", "text": "Applying a resource policy does not automatically remediate existing resources. Foojay’s August 13, 2025 walkthrough reports that an existing 0.0.0.0/0 entry remained and was flagged after a wildcard-blocking policy was applied. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/atlas-resource-policies.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Atlas nonCompliantResources endpoint"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://foojay.io/today/enforcing-governance-in-mongodb-atlas-with-resource-policies/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:0320a8ff506dc89ab56472dec931f5fddb4fabd7101e4f8addd28b61fcace06c", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:2130bec9e5770275ae965e72ff86e107115a350dea65651a08fcbbdc5bc0438c", "ev:29c9381619ca9acbba0d568f524dec11d6b70847e5b09b501ff1fb23c03e7cf3"]}
{"id": "clm:e9147f58c13beac1fffb422fcc15d7456fdf0c269262f05f79f437254ce8ec4f", "type": "statement", "text": "Existing autoscaling limits can permit automatic scaling beyond a newly applied policy even though manual scaling beyond policy limits is blocked. MongoDB recommends identifying these resources with nonCompliantResources and updating them. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-23)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/atlas-resource-policies.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Atlas nonCompliantResources endpoint"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:0320a8ff506dc89ab56472dec931f5fddb4fabd7101e4f8addd28b61fcace06c", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:ef1a81dc6f00984991f1d4e4a39a3b3c271ea0d685de5a752121d0a65f7c588b"]}
{"id": "clm:2d630744e038ff441cef480786853bf60d1974f7bbba0fbec4567967fe4f744c", "type": "statement", "text": "Integrate nonCompliantResources polling with configuration-drift monitoring and route returned resources to remediation; MongoDB recommends proactive monitoring, and How to Harden explicitly recommends wiring the query into drift alerting. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/atlas-resource-policies.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Atlas nonCompliantResources endpoint"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://howtoharden.com/guides/mongodb-atlas/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:0320a8ff506dc89ab56472dec931f5fddb4fabd7101e4f8addd28b61fcace06c", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:5044ae0b6ae91e3bc373353cc33b3ea1356268bdf9b231b802e6d3f0b4ede00e", "ev:5e5b9972d82be3ecd76b3282345dd989702f927178d185d1e9215bc9ec45c96d"]}
{"id": "clm:6e9efc41adfd1373b4f12e2c3186d300ecc6697fc12910a1379400e182f1a4fe", "type": "statement", "text": "The Resource Policies endpoint set shares an ORGANIZATION-scoped token bucket: capacity 500 and refill 250 tokens per 60 seconds. nonCompliantResources shares that bucket with resource-policy CRUD and validation endpoints. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-14)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/api/api-rate-limit.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Atlas nonCompliantResources endpoint"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:0320a8ff506dc89ab56472dec931f5fddb4fabd7101e4f8addd28b61fcace06c", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:5d7aed78030b39931015622cfa3480fa488dcfe476f1d8ea80eae7f472235649", "ev:d9f0c7a1300e3503195f875b87f307f6fb70bf769d9f6e6127ddf73bbf7cde33"]}
{"id": "clm:b89c34f7897d6aaabea0ad8a64681190d67593c84b2179832e1cf506626e7b41", "type": "statement", "text": "The API reference includes the CLI command atlas api resourcePolicies getNonCompliantResources --help and examples for bearer-token and HTTP Digest authentication. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-23)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/api/doc/atlas-admin-api-v2/operation/operation-getorgnoncompliantresources", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Atlas nonCompliantResources endpoint"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:0320a8ff506dc89ab56472dec931f5fddb4fabd7101e4f8addd28b61fcace06c", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:066d235e2cf3c8d51ce61cea71a8e231986a1fba3a9a3a2986ceff33627ebcde"]}
{"id": "clm:20c1483175b51adc90e31bc6b3e5beb137e6f645129cc6b1a4ad72528f5074df", "type": "statement", "text": "The API reference lists Organization Member as its role requirement and documents service-account bearer authentication and API-key Digest authentication examples. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-23)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/api/doc/atlas-admin-api-v2/operation/operation-getorgnoncompliantresources", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Atlas nonCompliantResources endpoint"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:0320a8ff506dc89ab56472dec931f5fddb4fabd7101e4f8addd28b61fcace06c", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:066d235e2cf3c8d51ce61cea71a8e231986a1fba3a9a3a2986ceff33627ebcde", "ev:b0b690cdc116e45874378065d2ee3220b35dbaf18c86ef53199a4e0b3ff8ba29"]}
{"id": "clm:ea1df20edd8fe6bf1bc5144cde17e338e3c5a8324b47b2a150009a3a12cd2135", "type": "statement", "text": "MongoDB recommends proactive monitoring: downstream failures can leave intermediate states non-compliant, and clusters with pre-existing autoscaling limits beyond a new policy can continue scaling automatically beyond those boundaries even though manual scaling is constrained. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-23)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/atlas-resource-policies.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Atlas nonCompliantResources endpoint"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:0320a8ff506dc89ab56472dec931f5fddb4fabd7101e4f8addd28b61fcace06c", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:5044ae0b6ae91e3bc373353cc33b3ea1356268bdf9b231b802e6d3f0b4ede00e", "ev:ef1a81dc6f00984991f1d4e4a39a3b3c271ea0d685de5a752121d0a65f7c588b"]}
{"id": "clm:54a86cfb113afa83382f9cc5b05e76dc2857eeb8b828ead5514135054409c176", "type": "statement", "text": "After an Atlas Resource Policy is applied, Atlas only allows changes to an existing non-compliant cluster that bring it into compliance; if the policy blocks AWS, MongoDB's example says the cluster can only be switched to Azure or Google Cloud. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-23)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/atlas-resource-policies.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Atlas nonCompliantResources endpoint"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/atlas-resource-policies/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:0320a8ff506dc89ab56472dec931f5fddb4fabd7101e4f8addd28b61fcace06c", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:12baf34fa4cbd4da8c5868c113de4d8c8eb5bc896665631a919ea61cb8f7560d"]}
